# Decimal remainder with integer operands

Takes 10.5 modulo 3 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays an exact decimal, producing 1.5 when the
decimal is the dividend and 1 when the integer is the dividend.

>>> source
decimal_value: decimal = 10.5
integer_divisor: int = 3
integer_dividend: int = 10
decimal_divisor: decimal = 3

// Verifies the Decimal/Int promotion with the decimal dividend first.
decimal_remainder: decimal = decimal_value % integer_divisor
print(decimal_remainder)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_remainder: decimal = integer_dividend % decimal_divisor
print(integer_remainder)

<<< stdout
1.5
1

<<< stderr
